1
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Brave young men who rode on the wings of victory.

2
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Memphis Belle is a drama, war, action film directed by Michael Caton-Jones.

3
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:09,000
The "Memphis Belle" is a World War II bomber, piloted by a
young crew on dangerous bombing raids into Europe.

4
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
The crew only have to make one more bombing raid before they
have finished their duty and can go home.

5
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
In the briefing before their last flight, the crew
discover that the target for the day is Bremen.

6
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Dennis Dearborn, played by Matthew Modine.

7
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Danny Daly, played by Eric Stoltz.

8
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Luke Sinclair, played by Tate Donovan.

9
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:15,000
Phil Lowenthal, played by D. B. Sweeney.

10
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Val Kozlowski, played by Billy Zane.

11
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:57,000
Richard "Rascal" Moore, played by Sean Astin.

12
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
Memphis Belle is a 1990 war drama film directed by Michael
Caton-Jones and written by Monte Merrick.

13
01:09:33,000 --> 01:09:39,000
The film stars Matthew Modine, Eric Stoltz, and Harry Connick Jr.

14
01:14:54,000 --> 01:15:00,000
(in his film debut).

15
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
Memphis Belle is a fictional version of the 1944 documentary Memphis Belle: A Story of a Flying Fortress by director William Wyler, about the
25th and last mission of an American Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress bomber, the Memphis Belle, based in England during World War II.

16
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
The 1990 version was co-produced by David Puttnam and Wyler's
daughter Catherine and dedicated to her father.

17
01:30:57,000 --> 01:31:03,000
The film closes with a dedication to all airmen, friend or foe, who
fought in the skies above Europe during World War II.

18
01:36:18,000 --> 01:36:24,000
The film explores themes of world war ii, bomber, u.s.
air force, danger of life, soldier.

19
01:41:39,000 --> 01:41:45,000
The tone is emotional.
